","workbench_component_id":"24dd602a-083e-5749-875d-7f272c8f58b7"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"0e08fd5e3cb4595473e0d59f066eac51d9cd028cfacabf0152eaebbb94e6bdcb","heading":null,"ordinal":19,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:19","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Marginal access streets” or “frontage roads” means a minor street which is generally parallel to or adjacent to a major traffic thoroughfare highway or railroad right-of-way and provides access to abutting properties.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"121f61ee-9ee5-567d-8118-be3fa901a680"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"a2abf1de46934938da267ade744d2286b32ca3d053160261822b7dbcd44aacb9","heading":null,"ordinal":20,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:20","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Master plan” means the comprehensive plan made and adopted by the Planning Commission for the physical development of the metropolitan area and its environs indicating the general location, character and extent of streets, alleys, sewers, ways, viaducts, bridges, subways, parkways, parks, playgrounds, waterways, waterfronts, boulevards, squares, aviation fields and other public ways, grounds and open spaces, the general location of public buildings and other public property, and the general location and extent of public utilities and terminals; also the removal, location, widening, narrowing, vacating, abandonment, change of use, or extension of any public ways, grounds, open spaces, buildings, property, utilities or terminals, as well as a zoning plan for the control of the height, area, bulk, location, use and intensity of use of buildings and premises.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"945aa0a1-a1c7-58f2-8bec-d57bad8dc26f"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"b6f35775a7a1d2872598d41770dd0c4d9f2b6a2f5ada8aec34357fba290e400d","heading":null,"ordinal":21,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:21","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Minor plat approval” means a plan or map of an area prepared in accordance with the provisions of this division and those of any other ordinance which requires only the joint approval of the Planning Director and Public Works Director.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"22e78ada-8914-5fa1-8fa0-e1c55b202707"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"807711d072d489cafd9723e372d2688357bb11f3371c60305fce95b767610b64","heading":null,"ordinal":22,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:22","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Minor street” means a street of limited continuity, which serves or is intended to serve the local needs of a neighborhood.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"83c41049-714f-5f29-9363-6926ccb06087"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"aff941d89fc4964c359ba6cbebb440932824858fd87f2a9b87aa4adacd11677f","heading":null,"ordinal":23,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:23","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Pedestrian way” means a right-of-way dedicated to public use, which cuts across a block to facilitate pedestrian access to adjacent streets and properties.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"60b800f2-aa80-51c4-b5f3-edd77d1fe444"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"1d7dc5f40f95b38f0a52635d31e8be90f8978f9148038b24b97f9ad8e2aef2b4","heading":null,"ordinal":24,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:24","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Planning Commission” means the City of Topeka Planning Commission.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"f9bfe74a-497a-549d-932c-a01f7fdbc105"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"a1731eeacdb30bc08e51c3818ae045c3d074874c8ba053a36e26260ac8629565","heading":null,"ordinal":25,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:25","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Preliminary plat” means a map made for the purpose of showing the design of a proposed subdivision and existing conditions in and around it; the map need not be based on an accurate or detailed final survey of the property.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"cf7cfec0-074b-551f-9eb9-99823d8364ad"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"56db6f841099419e3a062f87c090e1b1f0d93c440926d66f0a7877cfd93b5627","heading":null,"ordinal":26,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:26","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Public water company” means any person who has a written permit from the State to supply water for domestic purposes to the public.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"67e62e16-cba6-5621-86d8-68475c26d196"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"aa819c6d3ee3ede7ed856fc2f2a5a4b91a580f697d7c285d6aff894674c52921","heading":null,"ordinal":27,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:27","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Setback line” or “building line” means a line on a plat generally parallel to the street right-of-way, indicating the limit beyond which buildings or structures may not be erected or altered.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"e19e815e-a7a7-5722-a758-5bb9846e204c"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"ad58894850a281a9a406282f144f3f94debe239c0d6bb689a89d27eca4eb4090","heading":null,"ordinal":28,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:28","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Street” means a right-of-way dedicated to the public use, or a private right-of-way serving more than one owner, which provides principal vehicular and pedestrian access to adjacent properties.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"08ce835c-51db-5110-b159-98b460168910"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"9122b2fe4b9cd54832b58fa1a6936c384fddc80a806d033643821fab4020545c","heading":null,"ordinal":29,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:29","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Subdivider” means any person who causes land to be divided into a subdivision, for themselves or for others.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"db08748d-7f88-50e7-836d-5f2d0cc707d2"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"19d92d779980d13293e87b1b9edf5b29c4edcd4a18598054664a7beb1cdbcb1d","heading":null,"ordinal":30,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:30","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Subdivision” means the division of a parcel of land into two or more lots or parcels for the purpose of transfer of ownership or building development.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"cd332f18-9aa4-560b-a397-08cd62c28a5d"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"1d918eb3540a1b451473a9ddd5ad7054432fcc251d2458ca1235a154eab54e66","heading":null,"ordinal":31,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:31","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"“Urban growth area” means the area identified in the land use and growth management plan which is an element of the comprehensive plan. (Ord. 19942 § 1, 3-10-15.)","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"3d8c3cb8-b920-564c-9cf2-42391e39ddbe"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"06e14d0ebd52300a4940f01134a36eb0aa2b67f39a58c4b905cd742a8e257e8f","heading":null,"ordinal":32,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:block:32","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":"Cross References: Definitions generally, TMC 1.10.020 .","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"f4b8e730-6a5f-5f3d-b59a-b2c13d7a5533"},{"attributes":{"legacy_definition_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.30.010:def:alley"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","content_hash":"9dd828d226162bba6595cedcbfa47ca744ec2a57e1c4ebd1a45ef8d732248f51","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.30.010:definition:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.30.010","text":null,"type":"definition","workbench_component_id":"b68aa077-42ab-5b1e-b20d-f15b7d334242"},{"attributes":{"legacy_definition_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.30.010:def:block"},"citation":"18.30.010","citation_url":"https://top